      "end_seconds": 5.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Um, uh, sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.07,
      "end_seconds": 11.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "yes, have a seat tell me what's going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.34,
      "end_seconds": 29.13,
      "duration_seconds": 14.79,
      "text": "yeah, um, I wanted to get a bump on my head looked at i thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.57,
      "end_seconds": 33.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.58,
      "end_seconds": 46.28,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "It's been going on for about four days. Oh, and a headache since the fall. That's been about the same, two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.48,
      "end_seconds": 49.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.25,
      "end_seconds": 55.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Um, no, nothing at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.76,
      "end_seconds": 59.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.35,
      "end_seconds": 62.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "No, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.64,
      "end_seconds": 66.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.86,
      "end_seconds": 72.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "I had a varicose vein procedure last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.64,
      "end_seconds": 88.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "right, who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.19,
      "end_seconds": 92.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.61,
      "end_seconds": 95.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.24,
      "end_seconds": 100.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.06,
      "end_seconds": 106.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "So, what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.32,
      "end_seconds": 112.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.23,
      "end_seconds": 128.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "Have you had any clear fluid from the nose or ear, double vision or loss of consciousness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.66,
      "end_seconds": 135.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Well, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.8,
      "end_seconds": 137.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "How about vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.02,
      "end_seconds": 141.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Ah, not that I've noticed, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.3,
      "end_seconds": 145.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.69,
      "end_seconds": 150.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.23,
      "end_seconds": 156.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.97,
      "end_seconds": 160.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "no, nothing with my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.68,
      "end_seconds": 167.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.64,
      "end_seconds": 179.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Right, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.44,
      "end_seconds": 206.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "okay: BP is 122 over 82, pulse 64. And And saturation 99 percent, temperature is 36.4 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.13,
      "end_seconds": 209.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.39,
      "end_seconds": 214.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Alright, they help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.51,
      "end_seconds": 221.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.95,
      "end_seconds": 225.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.08,
      "end_seconds": 243.54,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "There is a small bruise on the forehead, the pupils are equal and reactive, and you are walking steadily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.85,
      "end_seconds": 259.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.4,
      "end_seconds": 297.04,
      "duration_seconds": 32.64,
      "text": "okay, that's enough for me. From what you've told me and what I found, my working impression is a minor head injury without worrying signs. Another possibility is a concussion. Let's use paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. You take it by mouth. It's for headache. Someone should stay with you tonight, and no alcohol or contact sport for now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.9,
      "end_seconds": 306.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Come back or go to emergency straight away if you vomit repeatedly, become drowsy or confused, or have a fit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.45,
      "end_seconds": 311.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Okay, you know, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.46,
      "end_seconds": 316.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.23,
      "end_seconds": 319.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
